<title>USA: Shell confirms Texaco merger talks.</title>
<headline>Shell confirms Texaco merger talks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Oil Co confirmed Monday that it is in talks with Texaco over a potential merger of its downstream operations.</p>
<p>&quot;Shell Oil Company confirms it is discussing with Texaco the potential for joint arrangements involving U.S. downstream operations,&quot; Shell said in a statement. &quot;While the companies are reviewing a range of options concerning the businesses that might be included, no decisions have been made.&quot;</p>
<p>The company was responding to a Wall Street Journal report Monday that Shell, Texaco and state-owned Saudi Aramco were in talks over a possible three-way merger.</p>
</text>
